WEBVTT

00:42.125 --> 00:45.963
MY ROYAL NEMESIS

00:46.046 --> 00:50.842
FIVE HOURS BEFORE THE FLIGHT

00:53.929 --> 00:55.556
You like Luwak coffee, Ms. Mo?

00:55.639 --> 00:56.932
Yes, I do.

00:57.015 --> 00:59.101
I enjoy it as a drip brew sometimes.

00:59.184 --> 01:00.561
What about you?

01:00.644 --> 01:01.562
I used to,

01:01.645 --> 01:03.772
until a business trip
to Bali three years ago.

01:03.855 --> 01:06.316
I went for a raw materials survey
and caught the first flight back.

01:06.400 --> 01:07.401
Why?

01:07.484 --> 01:09.236
It just rubbed me the wrong way.

01:09.736 --> 01:12.447
That expensive coffee
is made from cat poop, after all.

01:13.699 --> 01:15.993
I couldn't drink it
once I saw it for myself.

01:16.076 --> 01:18.370
The same applies here.
I could have dated you in ignorance,

01:18.453 --> 01:21.665
but the truth won't allow it now, you see.

01:22.541 --> 01:24.126
It sounds like you're upset.

01:24.209 --> 01:25.836
Marriage is a lifelong business.

01:25.919 --> 01:27.879
Shouldn't trust be paramount?

01:29.298 --> 01:31.341
You should pay for the coffee.

01:31.967 --> 01:33.719
Let's call it a damages settlement.

01:34.886 --> 01:36.597
-Hold on.
-Right.

01:38.140 --> 01:40.684
Just a heads up.
You should go somewhere else for lunch.

01:40.767 --> 01:42.978
I have a blind date
on the second floor in ten minutes.

01:43.061 --> 01:45.147
I'm all about efficiency,

01:45.230 --> 01:47.107
so I figured I'd kill two birds
with one stone.

01:47.190 --> 01:48.609
Don't be too offended.

01:58.994 --> 02:00.120
Se-gye!

02:01.371 --> 02:02.623
That blind date

02:03.248 --> 02:04.499
is with me.

02:05.334 --> 02:07.294
Give me a chance to apologize properly.

02:09.379 --> 02:10.380
What's going on here?

02:10.464 --> 02:13.884
I fail to see why you must insist
on this union.

02:15.177 --> 02:17.012
Mochang's value-driven approach

02:17.095 --> 02:18.513
and Chail's formidable tech assets

02:18.597 --> 02:20.474
would make a perfectly synergistic pair.

02:20.557 --> 02:22.017
When the need is this great,

02:22.100 --> 02:24.728
even broken trust might be
worth rebuilding.

02:25.854 --> 02:27.230
You've never lost, have you?

02:27.898 --> 02:29.858
No. I don't recall
any losses in particular.

02:29.941 --> 02:32.611
You've never known defeat or loss.

02:32.694 --> 02:35.447
Life isn't particularly easy,
but it's not too hard either.

02:35.530 --> 02:38.200
Even so, you're only satisfied
when you get what you need.

02:38.283 --> 02:40.118
Is that a bad thing?

02:41.495 --> 02:42.913
Not necessarily.

02:45.165 --> 02:48.168
I can't stand people who don't know jack,
meddle in everything,

02:48.251 --> 02:52.255
and insist on wallowing
in their entitlement.

02:56.385 --> 02:59.137
Since it appears you're a woman
who shares my values,

02:59.221 --> 03:02.891
I guess we can skip
the needless mind games and runaround.

03:08.772 --> 03:10.941
You're toxic, like poison.

03:12.150 --> 03:13.110
Cha Se-gye!

03:13.193 --> 03:14.236
Have you gone mad?

03:14.861 --> 03:16.738
Cha Se-gye! Open your eyes!

03:16.822 --> 03:19.866
I can't stand people who don't know jack,
meddle in everything…

03:21.493 --> 03:24.955
and insist on wallowing
in their entitlement.

03:25.038 --> 03:27.749
-Cha Se-gye, no!
-One, two, three!

03:36.550 --> 03:37.906
Oh no…

03:38.593 --> 03:41.221
Since it appears you're a woman
who shares my values,

03:42.055 --> 03:43.807
I guess we can skip

03:44.391 --> 03:46.977
the needless mind games and runaround.

03:51.857 --> 03:52.816
Passengers,

03:52.899 --> 03:56.069
we will soon be arriving
at Jeju International Airport.

03:56.153 --> 03:57.696
Please fasten your seatbelts…

03:59.740 --> 04:01.283
No feelings, my foot.

04:03.702 --> 04:07.330
EPISODE 6
ONE MAGICAL NIGHT

04:17.007 --> 04:18.425
All white walls

04:19.050 --> 04:21.303
and nothing but white everywhere…

04:22.012 --> 04:23.054
Could this be…

04:23.138 --> 04:24.556
Have I finally…

04:26.725 --> 04:29.186
crossed over to the afterlife?

04:32.689 --> 04:33.857
I see no hellfire.

04:35.317 --> 04:37.778
No King of Hell either.

04:39.654 --> 04:40.947
Paradise?

04:44.201 --> 04:45.327
My goodness!

04:45.827 --> 04:47.287
No, I am in hell.

04:49.247 --> 04:50.457
Oh no…

04:51.208 --> 04:53.335
Hey. Are you awake?

04:54.795 --> 04:56.421
I see I am still alive.

04:56.505 --> 04:58.882
Man, you really scared me.

04:59.674 --> 05:01.551
Who gets electrocuted on a plane?

05:02.135 --> 05:04.179
Talk about a hardcore first day.

05:04.262 --> 05:06.389
We are still alive, so cease your fussing.

05:07.516 --> 05:08.683
What of Cha Se-gye?

05:08.767 --> 05:10.268
What has become of Cha Se-gye?

05:10.894 --> 05:14.523
Your pre-flight medication
didn't contain the substance,

05:14.606 --> 05:17.818
but your blood test indicates
digitoxin poisoning,

05:17.901 --> 05:19.986
resulting in acute cardiac arrest.

05:20.070 --> 05:21.238
Is that a poison?

05:21.321 --> 05:24.658
It is a digitalis-extracted compound
primarily used as a cardiac stimulant.

05:24.741 --> 05:28.119
It's used to treat heart failure,
arrhythmia, and epilepsy.

05:28.203 --> 05:31.331
We've administered the antidote,
so just rest up for a day,

05:31.414 --> 05:34.751
and you should be able to resume
daily activities without any issue.

05:34.835 --> 05:35.836
What about…

05:36.753 --> 05:37.838
What about her?

05:38.380 --> 05:39.840
-Is she okay?
-Who exactly?

05:39.923 --> 05:42.509
A woman should've been brought in with me.

05:42.592 --> 05:43.468
Shin Seo-ri.

05:43.552 --> 05:46.471
I'll look into it and let you know.

05:47.889 --> 05:48.974
Hold on.

05:50.475 --> 05:51.685
Oh my gosh.

05:52.185 --> 05:53.311
What?

05:53.395 --> 05:55.730
They're doing a CT, an MRI,
and even drawing blood?

05:56.857 --> 05:57.983
Blood?

05:58.066 --> 05:59.317
You cannot have my blood!

05:59.401 --> 06:01.319
Who knows what you will use it for?

06:01.862 --> 06:03.738
We'll use it for your health checkup.

06:05.699 --> 06:06.992
She is something else.

06:08.118 --> 06:10.579
We just had the first-class passengers
sign notarized NDAs,

06:10.662 --> 06:12.289
and their compensation
has been paid out.

06:12.372 --> 06:14.875
Good thing weekday flights are quiet.
We're bleeding money.

06:14.958 --> 06:17.043
Sir, you should request
a proper police investigation.

06:17.127 --> 06:18.795
It's not just rumors anymore.

06:18.879 --> 06:21.172
They bribed a nurse to drug you this time.

06:21.256 --> 06:22.507
You were in real danger.

06:22.591 --> 06:24.134
For someone in my position,

06:24.217 --> 06:26.094
this kind of threat is all too common.

06:26.177 --> 06:28.305
I can't be terrified every time.

06:28.388 --> 06:30.181
The moment I show my fear,

06:30.265 --> 06:31.474
it's game over for me.

06:31.558 --> 06:33.101
Even so, some people need to know.

06:33.184 --> 06:34.936
Hiding this even from your doctor friend--

06:35.020 --> 06:36.521
Isn't that a given?

06:36.605 --> 06:38.064
He could've been bought off.

06:38.148 --> 06:39.107
Lead with suspicion.

06:39.190 --> 06:40.358
By that logic,

06:40.942 --> 06:43.361
isn't Ms. Shin Seo-ri the most suspicious?

06:44.195 --> 06:45.655
Shin Seo-ri?

06:47.324 --> 06:48.825
-What about her?
-Just think about it.

06:48.909 --> 06:51.828
You two met over a fender bender,
then came an assault, investor problems,

06:51.912 --> 06:54.372
a police summons,
and now corporate shakedown rumors.

06:54.456 --> 06:57.417
It looks like she straight-up brought
calamity into your life.

06:57.500 --> 06:58.877
I'll give you the fender bender,

06:58.960 --> 07:01.713
but the rest has
absolutely nothing to do with her.

07:02.339 --> 07:03.757
Mr. Son.

07:03.840 --> 07:04.841
Yes, sir.

07:04.925 --> 07:07.761
You are an executive aide.
Your job is to deliver the facts.

07:08.511 --> 07:09.679
Yes, sir.

07:10.555 --> 07:11.514
Sir.

07:16.353 --> 07:18.730
I guess I'm just the big old jerk
in this scenario.

07:18.813 --> 07:20.023
Unbelievable.

07:20.106 --> 07:22.692
What a stand-up guy he is.

07:23.276 --> 07:25.779
They said there's
nothing seriously wrong with her.

07:25.862 --> 07:27.697
She's good to go after an IV drip.

07:27.781 --> 07:29.699
Must have been quite the shock
on your first day.

07:29.783 --> 07:31.242
It's Gwang-nam, right?

07:31.326 --> 07:34.663
I heard you two are close, like siblings.
Please take good care of her.

07:34.746 --> 07:36.915
I'll head down
after my meetings in Seoul.

07:36.998 --> 07:39.125
I think there's been
a huge misunderstanding,

07:39.209 --> 07:40.710
so let me clear it up right now.

07:40.794 --> 07:42.212
We are not like siblings at all.

07:42.295 --> 07:43.797
It's strictly business between us.

07:43.880 --> 07:45.131
And I'm not staying long.

07:45.215 --> 07:47.258
It's just a temp job
until I get a real one.

07:47.342 --> 07:50.053
You should start looking
for a replacement right away.

07:53.515 --> 07:54.683
Damn it.

07:56.393 --> 07:59.562
Leave it to her
to hire someone exactly like her.

07:59.646 --> 08:01.147
Why? What did her manager say?

08:01.231 --> 08:04.150
He said he's just a temp
and told me to replace him.

08:04.234 --> 08:06.444
He's really drawing
a bold line in the sand.

08:06.528 --> 08:07.862
Birds of a feather flock together.

08:07.946 --> 08:09.906
Can you blame him?

08:09.990 --> 08:11.574
Look at who he works for.

08:11.650 --> 08:13.777
I wondered why the pushover
suddenly grew a spine.

08:13.875 --> 08:15.704
Turns out there was a good reason.

08:15.787 --> 08:17.163
What reason?

08:18.081 --> 08:19.582
It looked like

08:19.666 --> 08:21.918
that loser hooked a rich boyfriend.

08:22.002 --> 08:24.295
Although I'm not sure if he's
a boyfriend or a sugar daddy.

08:25.630 --> 08:26.506
Okay.

08:28.216 --> 08:30.719
You're good to proceed
with the ad campaign now.

08:30.802 --> 08:31.720
I'm off.

08:36.307 --> 08:38.351
What blind idiot would go for her?

08:38.435 --> 08:40.145
My ideal type?

08:40.228 --> 08:43.732
A man like Hugh Grant in Notting Hill.

08:43.815 --> 08:46.693
He's practically every woman's dream.

08:46.776 --> 08:49.612
Yoon Ji-hyo's manager is so lucky.

08:49.696 --> 08:52.073
He gets paid to go
to a free fan meeting every day.

08:52.991 --> 08:55.452
If I were her manager,
I'd totally work for free.

08:55.535 --> 08:57.579
They'll all recognize you in Jeju.

08:57.662 --> 09:00.290
Maybe I could look into flights
to Taiwan or Japan

09:00.373 --> 09:02.208
that leave today instead?

09:02.292 --> 09:04.044
Everyone will recognize you in Jeju.

09:04.127 --> 09:07.088
Taiwan is where that jerk Gong Tae-woo
and I celebrated our first anniversary.

09:07.172 --> 09:10.550
Japan is where we had
that Christmas birthday event.

09:11.718 --> 09:12.594
Don't worry.

09:12.677 --> 09:15.930
I rented out
an entire private resort anyway.

09:16.431 --> 09:18.308
I won't be running into anyone there.

09:18.391 --> 09:21.603
HALLA GENERAL HOSPITAL

09:32.405 --> 09:33.823
Listen here.

09:33.907 --> 09:35.825
Where is the one named Cha Se-gye?

09:35.909 --> 09:37.077
How can I help you?

09:37.160 --> 09:38.745
I have come to see him.

09:38.828 --> 09:39.954
Lead the way.

09:40.830 --> 09:42.040
What's with her tone…

09:43.041 --> 09:45.585
Miss, may I have your name first?

09:45.668 --> 09:46.628
Why do you need my name?

09:48.088 --> 09:50.131
I don't think you should be
wandering alone just yet.

09:50.215 --> 09:51.549
Don't go anywhere.

09:51.633 --> 09:52.926
Just stay put for now.

09:53.009 --> 09:53.968
How dare you!

09:54.511 --> 09:56.262
You have yet to answer my question.

09:57.263 --> 09:58.973
Is this the psych ward?

09:59.974 --> 10:03.144
-Listen here, I have a question.
-Yes?

10:03.228 --> 10:05.897
Do you know where the one named
Cha Se-gye is convalescing?

10:05.980 --> 10:07.482
Pardon me? "Convalescing"?

10:07.565 --> 10:10.652
Miss, do you happen to remember
which room you're in?

10:10.735 --> 10:13.696
Is giving nonsensical answers
the physicians' specialty at this clinic?

10:13.780 --> 10:15.824
Everybody refuses to answer my questions.

10:15.907 --> 10:17.951
Just stay right here.

10:19.160 --> 10:22.038
Why do you all keep telling me
to stay still like a sack of grain!

10:22.122 --> 10:23.206
Shin Seo-ri.

10:34.509 --> 10:37.846
The media response to the groundbreaking
of Songjin Resort has been positive.

10:37.929 --> 10:39.806
Let's wrap up
the foundation work this year.

10:39.889 --> 10:41.349
Once it's completed in 2029,

10:41.432 --> 10:44.644
I trust Chail Food will handle
the F&amp;B operations well.

10:44.727 --> 10:47.564
Thanks to that, we're finally seeing
some green after a long time.

10:47.647 --> 10:49.399
The shareholders are very pleased.

10:49.482 --> 10:50.942
Thanks to Mun-do,

10:51.025 --> 10:53.486
you can finally hold your head up
in front of your shareholders.

10:53.570 --> 10:56.197
Ever since the accounting fraud
sent their stock tanking,

10:56.281 --> 10:57.782
they've been absolutely miserable.

10:57.866 --> 10:59.242
Without even lifting a finger.

10:59.325 --> 11:01.035
It's a total win-win.

11:07.625 --> 11:10.461
CHA SE-GYE FAINTS ON FLIGHT TO JEJU
RECOVERING IN JEJU HOSPITAL

11:21.514 --> 11:22.557
Are you truly all right?

11:22.640 --> 11:24.767
Stop fussing. You're giving me a headache.

11:25.310 --> 11:28.354
You must truly be okay after all
if you're still able to be this cranky.

11:28.438 --> 11:30.773
I'm not okay at all, you clueless woman.

11:30.857 --> 11:32.358
Why not just stay out of the way?

11:32.442 --> 11:34.485
I very nearly died thanks to you.

11:34.569 --> 11:36.446
People do not die that easily.

11:36.529 --> 11:39.115
I speak from extensive experience
with near-death events.

11:39.199 --> 11:41.743
The thread of life is
surprisingly tough, like steel.

11:41.826 --> 11:44.704
Unless your time has come,
it does not snap easily.

11:44.787 --> 11:46.539
Spare me the cheap philosophy.

11:46.623 --> 11:48.041
Why are you here?

11:48.917 --> 11:50.043
I am not here for you.

11:51.419 --> 11:52.837
I was just passing through.

11:52.921 --> 11:54.881
The VIP ward is nowhere
near the first-floor ER.

11:54.964 --> 11:57.300
There's no way
you were just passing through.

12:02.889 --> 12:05.225
Looks like you were
pretty worried about me.

12:05.975 --> 12:07.268
Worried?

12:09.395 --> 12:11.105
Of course I was worried.

12:11.189 --> 12:12.440
If the money man goes down,

12:12.523 --> 12:14.150
my prospects naturally go down with him.

12:14.234 --> 12:15.693
I had no choice but to worry.

12:16.236 --> 12:19.072
That's enough.
Spare me your capitalist concerns.

12:19.739 --> 12:21.658
There you are, Mr. Cha.

12:21.741 --> 12:25.328
We've forwarded the detailed results
to your primary physician,

12:25.411 --> 12:27.413
so you may be discharged immediately
as requested.

12:27.497 --> 12:28.539
Thank you.

12:28.623 --> 12:30.375
And regarding that patient

12:30.458 --> 12:32.460
you asked about earlier…

12:32.543 --> 12:34.295
Hold on. You go in here for a second.

12:34.379 --> 12:35.338
Why?

12:35.421 --> 12:37.507
Don't argue. Just go.

12:40.051 --> 12:41.761
-Please continue.
-According to the results,

12:41.844 --> 12:44.222
Ms. Shin Seo-ri has
no major health issues.

12:45.181 --> 12:46.349
Nothing to worry about.

12:47.225 --> 12:48.643
-I see.
-Yes. Take care.

12:56.401 --> 12:57.860
Goodness me.

13:01.864 --> 13:04.951
That flying palanquin was split
into beggar and commoner sections.

13:05.034 --> 13:07.245
It seems this clinic is no different.

13:09.831 --> 13:12.083
My goodness. It is so big.

13:12.166 --> 13:14.294
FOR A FLIRTY MOOD

13:17.505 --> 13:18.464
There.

13:21.467 --> 13:22.343
Cha Se-gye.

13:22.427 --> 13:25.263
I thought your complexion
had gone from deathly to radiant.

13:25.346 --> 13:27.432
-Now I see why.
-What is it now?

13:28.099 --> 13:29.934
This room is an absolute palace.

13:30.601 --> 13:31.477
We're both patients,

13:31.561 --> 13:34.147
yet they have me cooped up in a shoebox.

13:34.230 --> 13:35.773
This room has everything.

13:35.857 --> 13:37.734
Did you think we were on the same level?

13:37.817 --> 13:39.944
Just look at the size of that TV.

13:40.945 --> 13:42.822
And the sound quality is superb!

13:42.905 --> 13:45.241
Hey, that's too loud. Turn it down.

13:45.325 --> 13:47.118
Let me enjoy this palace too!

13:47.201 --> 13:49.245
-Not a chance.
-Hand it over, now!

13:49.329 --> 13:50.830
Try to take it.

13:52.248 --> 13:53.750
-What's wrong with you?
-Come on!

13:55.168 --> 13:56.711
Don't use force. Hey, wait a minute.

13:56.794 --> 13:58.254
We're going to fall. Hold on…

14:00.340 --> 14:01.257
Hey.

14:01.341 --> 14:03.301
-Let me watch some TV too!
-Hey!

14:03.968 --> 14:05.178
Stop that.

14:05.261 --> 14:06.679
Hey!

14:27.200 --> 14:29.118
WARMTH OF THE CANOLA FLOWER FIELD

14:34.832 --> 14:36.167
Oh my.

14:36.250 --> 14:39.045
I think I have the wrong room…

14:39.128 --> 14:41.089
No, I just have terrible timing.

14:47.929 --> 14:48.971
No.

14:50.056 --> 14:51.307
It's not what it looks like.

14:51.391 --> 14:53.351
I definitely knocked,

14:53.434 --> 14:54.477
but not hard enough.

14:54.560 --> 14:57.105
Since you hate loud noises so much,

14:57.188 --> 14:59.607
I just knocked lightly like I always do.

14:59.690 --> 15:01.943
If I had known a lady…
I mean, Ms. Shin Seo-ri was here,

15:02.026 --> 15:04.862
I should've knocked harder. Darn it.

15:04.946 --> 15:07.115
What are you talking about?

15:07.740 --> 15:10.076
This was… just an accident.

15:11.369 --> 15:13.704
It was like… a car accident.

15:13.788 --> 15:15.081
Yes… Right.

15:15.748 --> 15:17.792
As the old proverb goes,

15:17.875 --> 15:19.043
"Do not take your shoes off

15:19.127 --> 15:22.046
in a cucumber patch, and do not adjust
your hat string under a pear tree."

15:22.130 --> 15:24.841
It looks suspicious
to any onlooker, but this is…

15:24.924 --> 15:25.883
just a coincidence.

15:27.218 --> 15:30.179
Save the rambling explanation.
You're just making it weirder.

15:30.263 --> 15:31.681
Was I?

15:31.764 --> 15:32.974
I was trying my best.

15:33.057 --> 15:34.183
I'll come back later.

15:34.267 --> 15:36.018
-Don't go!
-Freeze!

15:46.571 --> 15:47.697
Damn it.

15:48.990 --> 15:50.700
That nearly scared me to death.

15:50.783 --> 15:52.952
That wicked creature.

15:55.872 --> 15:56.789
Is it all done?

15:56.873 --> 15:59.125
I made sure to keep
the passengers quiet.

15:59.208 --> 16:00.710
And your discharge is all sorted.

16:00.793 --> 16:01.961
Good work.

16:04.088 --> 16:06.507
I'll get changed and head out,
so be on standby.

16:07.175 --> 16:09.010
Sir, don't you think
you should stay a day

16:09.093 --> 16:10.928
and see how you feel?

16:11.012 --> 16:12.388
My test results are fine.

16:12.889 --> 16:15.391
Even if they weren't,
discharge is unavoidable.

16:15.475 --> 16:17.226
If we throw
health scare rumors into the mix,

16:17.310 --> 16:20.480
investors will demand
their money back before the launch.

16:22.398 --> 16:23.649
That's true.

16:24.275 --> 16:25.818
What about the other thing?

16:25.902 --> 16:28.779
After the shareholders' meeting,
President Choi is carrying out

16:28.863 --> 16:30.907
his schedule as planned.

16:31.532 --> 16:33.951
He must've been briefed
on my condition by now.

16:34.952 --> 16:35.912
Perfectly healthy.

16:35.995 --> 16:37.121
So,

16:37.914 --> 16:40.041
you really think
President Choi is behind this?

16:40.124 --> 16:41.959
Who else has the guts

16:42.043 --> 16:44.045
to pull off something like this?

16:46.255 --> 16:47.590
The deepfake,

16:48.257 --> 16:50.468
the attack, the rumors…

16:50.551 --> 16:53.304
And most importantly,
the Kaiserman private equity fund.

16:53.387 --> 16:54.805
All evidence points to him.

16:54.889 --> 16:57.099
He doesn't even seem to be hiding it.

16:57.183 --> 16:59.185
I'm not sure if he's just confident…

17:02.104 --> 17:03.648
or if he has a massive ego.

17:12.573 --> 17:13.950
Good work, everyone.

17:26.796 --> 17:28.965
Mr. Cha had the airline
and all the passengers

17:29.048 --> 17:30.841
sign notarized NDAs.

17:30.925 --> 17:32.969
Should we offer to pay the penalty
if they talk to us?

17:33.052 --> 17:34.637
Just make contact for now.

17:34.720 --> 17:36.347
We don't want needless chatter

17:36.430 --> 17:37.974
tanking the group's stock.

17:38.057 --> 17:39.392
Block any related articles.

17:40.142 --> 17:41.769
-For now.
-Just for now?

17:41.852 --> 17:44.230
Cha Se-gye must know by now.

17:44.814 --> 17:47.441
How far I'm willing to go for Chail

17:47.525 --> 17:49.026
and what I'm aiming for.

17:50.361 --> 17:51.862
It's a mental game from here on out.

17:51.946 --> 17:53.781
Whoever backs down first loses.

18:12.341 --> 18:14.594
-You really haven't seen her?
-I haven't.

18:15.511 --> 18:18.055
Where did she go?
I'm about to lose it.

18:18.681 --> 18:21.809
Hey, where did you go without telling me?

18:21.892 --> 18:24.478
Must I report my every move to you?

18:25.021 --> 18:26.689
When a master leaves the premises,

18:26.772 --> 18:29.817
it is the servant's duty
to wait quietly for her return.

18:29.900 --> 18:32.236
You still need to tell me,
so I don't worry.

18:32.320 --> 18:34.739
You were worried
about your money, not me.

18:35.823 --> 18:37.700
Cease your fretting and prepare to leave.

18:37.783 --> 18:39.493
You know our destination, yes?

18:39.577 --> 18:40.453
Discharging already?

18:40.536 --> 18:42.371
I have secured an iron palanquin for us,

18:42.455 --> 18:43.581
so come along.

18:44.206 --> 18:45.124
Iron palanquin?

18:52.298 --> 18:54.133
Mr. Son, what exactly is going on here?

18:54.216 --> 18:57.261
Well, the ad agency must have
booked the whole place.

18:57.345 --> 18:59.472
Turns out they're staying
at the same resort.

18:59.555 --> 19:01.057
They asked for a ride.

19:01.140 --> 19:02.850
This isn't an airport shuttle.

19:02.933 --> 19:05.269
You can't just let anyone ride with us.

19:05.353 --> 19:07.146
Must you be so unyielding?

19:07.813 --> 19:09.690
We can keep you company
on this lonely journey

19:09.774 --> 19:11.317
and fill these empty seats.

19:11.400 --> 19:12.735
Kill two birds with one stone.

19:12.818 --> 19:14.403
I never asked for company.

19:14.487 --> 19:17.698
We should've just rented a car
to avoid this being so awkward.

19:17.782 --> 19:19.742
I do not trust
your palanquin-driving skills,

19:19.825 --> 19:21.118
so hold your tongue.

19:21.786 --> 19:22.995
I'm sorry to interrupt,

19:23.079 --> 19:25.164
but can we stop at a rest area?

19:25.247 --> 19:26.999
Already? It hasn't even been five minutes.

19:27.083 --> 19:29.251
Well, I drank a latte on the plane,

19:29.335 --> 19:32.713
and it's making my stomach
rumble like crazy.

19:32.797 --> 19:34.882
You're lactose intolerant.

19:34.965 --> 19:36.676
Why would you drink a latte?

19:37.510 --> 19:38.386
Oh man.

19:38.469 --> 19:41.013
-Lactose intolerance?
-Wait, could this be…

19:41.097 --> 19:42.932
If we throw
health scare rumors into the mix,

19:43.015 --> 19:45.851
investors will demand
their money back before the launch.

19:46.394 --> 19:47.269
"Health scare"?

19:47.937 --> 19:50.189
One collapses backward,

19:50.272 --> 19:52.024
and the other's stomach is rumbling.

19:52.108 --> 19:55.486
Chest pain, fainting,
and now dysentery too.

19:55.569 --> 19:56.779
These sound like the symptoms…

19:56.862 --> 19:58.531
Could it be a plague?

19:58.614 --> 20:01.075
Halt this iron palanquin.
Stop the car right now!

20:01.158 --> 20:02.118
What's wrong now?

20:02.201 --> 20:03.202
-Seo-ri.
-Are you carsick?

20:03.285 --> 20:05.079
I am going to get out now.
Stop the car at once!

20:05.162 --> 20:06.664
-No! Please…
-We can't just stop

20:06.747 --> 20:08.165
in the middle of the road. Just wait.

20:08.249 --> 20:10.668
The plague is far worse
than any tiger or smallpox!

20:10.763 --> 20:12.586
This is tantamount to suicide!

20:12.670 --> 20:13.921
Manager Baek! Open the door!

20:14.004 --> 20:14.922
-Okay.
-Open the door!

20:15.005 --> 20:16.215
-Don't open it.
-Someone help!

20:16.298 --> 20:18.300
Help! It is the plague! The plague!

20:18.384 --> 20:19.677
Someone help me!

20:22.638 --> 20:23.639
It is the plague!

20:25.558 --> 20:26.976
Did you really just throw a fit

20:27.059 --> 20:29.186
in the middle of the road
to save yourself?

20:29.729 --> 20:31.605
I had no other choice.

20:32.606 --> 20:35.985
If not poison, the symptoms matched
the plague perfectly.

20:36.068 --> 20:37.361
What else was I supposed to do?

20:37.445 --> 20:39.029
You hitched a ride, offering "company,"

20:39.113 --> 20:41.365
but I guess a plague changes everything.

20:41.449 --> 20:43.159
You do not know
the true terror of a plague.

20:43.242 --> 20:45.703
Once infected, it spares no one,

20:45.786 --> 20:46.954
be it a king or a commoner.

20:53.419 --> 20:57.798
I see now. So is that why
you maintain such a great distance?

20:57.882 --> 20:59.842
"Hope for the best,
prepare for the worst."

20:59.925 --> 21:02.803
It is always best
to be prepared for anything.

21:03.554 --> 21:06.766
From now on,
I shall do nothing but breathe.

21:07.475 --> 21:10.227
Think of me as a sack of barley,
and pay me no mind.

21:10.770 --> 21:14.023
A plague fighter to a sack of barley.
One hell of a switch in attitude.

21:15.065 --> 21:18.068
Sir, we should get going.
The sun is setting.

21:18.569 --> 21:21.947
For dysentery of unknown cause,
cranesbill is a surefire remedy.

21:22.031 --> 21:24.033
Cranesbill petals have three stripes,

21:24.116 --> 21:25.159
while geraniums have five.

21:25.242 --> 21:26.869
Do not confuse them.

21:26.952 --> 21:28.621
Look at our Joseon-era doctor over here.

21:28.704 --> 21:32.374
Your meddling stretches
as far as the Great Wall.

21:33.000 --> 21:35.085
Why are you nitpicking
every little thing today?

21:35.169 --> 21:38.172
Just because I rejected your affections,
you hound me all damn day?

21:38.255 --> 21:39.173
Oh my goodness.

21:39.256 --> 21:40.716
What do you think you're doing?

21:40.800 --> 21:43.511
Are you trying to broadcast
your rejection of me to the whole world?

21:43.594 --> 21:44.595
Jeez.

21:45.179 --> 21:46.514
You'd better stop.

21:46.597 --> 21:47.473
Let's go.

21:47.973 --> 21:48.974
Get in, hurry.

21:55.147 --> 21:57.191
It might look like nothing special,

21:57.274 --> 21:58.818
but this tree is a handful to maintain.

21:58.901 --> 21:59.985
-You see…
-Father?

22:00.069 --> 22:00.945
Hey.

22:01.028 --> 22:02.321
Hello.

22:02.404 --> 22:03.739
I'm Mo Tae-hee.

22:03.823 --> 22:05.449
She went on a blind date with Se-gye.

22:05.533 --> 22:07.326
The third daughter of the Mochang Group.

22:08.285 --> 22:10.496
-Is that so?
-You must be the second aunt.

22:10.579 --> 22:14.208
Thanks to you, Mochang Woolen
is forever stuck in second place.

22:14.291 --> 22:16.335
Well, latecomers don't have
much of a choice.

22:16.418 --> 22:18.879
Father, did you hear about Se-gye?

22:19.421 --> 22:20.506
Yes.

22:20.589 --> 22:22.716
I was so shocked on my way here.

22:23.425 --> 22:25.469
So, I was thinking we should
ask outsiders to leave

22:25.553 --> 22:27.179
and talk among ourselves.

22:27.263 --> 22:28.931
I heard the news too.

22:29.014 --> 22:31.225
A small incident on the plane.

22:31.308 --> 22:32.726
-An incident?
-Yes.

22:32.810 --> 22:35.938
Fortunately, they handled it quickly
and resumed their schedule.

22:36.021 --> 22:36.981
Se-gye said that?

22:37.064 --> 22:38.983
I was surprised too,

22:39.066 --> 22:42.570
but she came by to reassure me
that it was nothing to worry about.

22:42.653 --> 22:44.905
You must have been
very worried about Se-gye.

22:44.989 --> 22:46.407
Seeing how you rushed right over.

22:46.490 --> 22:49.451
I thought he'd be lonely
growing up without a mother,

22:49.535 --> 22:51.745
but he's lucky to have an aunt like you.

22:53.497 --> 22:54.415
Yes.

22:54.498 --> 22:56.709
I have cleaned up a lot of his messes.

22:58.294 --> 22:59.378
What's this?

22:59.461 --> 23:01.005
I thought you went home.

23:01.547 --> 23:03.507
Hello. You must be the eldest aunt.

23:03.591 --> 23:04.925
It's a pleasure to meet you.

23:05.009 --> 23:06.093
I'm Mo Tae-hee.

23:06.176 --> 23:07.636
Okay. Nice to meet you.

23:12.474 --> 23:14.143
May I visit again?

23:14.226 --> 23:15.686
You both seem so lovely.

23:15.769 --> 23:17.563
I'd love to see you more often.

23:30.117 --> 23:31.452
Visiting Jeju Island for work.

23:31.535 --> 23:32.912
Even the sky welcomes me.

23:33.537 --> 23:35.456
Should I report this or not?

23:42.588 --> 23:44.882
The road is quite bumpy. Hold on tight.

23:49.345 --> 23:52.014
She's actually shut up.
Finally, some peace and quiet.

23:56.769 --> 23:59.563
Threatened by an assassin
in broad daylight.

23:59.647 --> 24:01.482
Why are you sprawled out like this?

24:01.565 --> 24:03.984
And he just collapsed,
despite being in perfect health.

24:09.573 --> 24:10.449
Mr. Son.

24:10.532 --> 24:12.159
Try to drive more carefully.

24:14.119 --> 24:15.120
Gosh.

24:15.788 --> 24:17.373
Come on now.

24:21.168 --> 24:22.044
Ms. Shin.

24:22.127 --> 24:24.046
You should be friends with Cha Se-gye.

24:24.630 --> 24:28.217
Is that man wearing the king's face
the poisonous influence in your life,

24:28.300 --> 24:29.510
not mine?

24:29.593 --> 24:31.679
Your luck with people rivals mine.

24:33.138 --> 24:35.307
Jesus, you startled me.
What are you staring at?

24:35.391 --> 24:38.435
Are you absolutely certain
you didn't swallow poison?

24:39.311 --> 24:41.981
Who's being poisoned in the 21st century?

24:42.982 --> 24:45.359
If it isn't a plague or poison,

24:45.442 --> 24:46.902
how does a healthy man--

24:46.986 --> 24:48.779
It's just chronic fatigue. So what?

24:50.280 --> 24:52.449
What good is a man so frail?

24:52.533 --> 24:54.451
Who are you calling frail? I'm…

24:56.745 --> 24:59.039
You have no idea
how much I can squat.

24:59.123 --> 25:00.916
You are all talk.

25:01.500 --> 25:02.918
Look. The ocean.

25:12.261 --> 25:14.388
Well, Mr. Cha's office

25:14.471 --> 25:16.765
won't stop calling me.

25:16.849 --> 25:18.851
I can't keep pretending I'm not home.

25:18.934 --> 25:20.019
When can I stop hiding?

25:20.102 --> 25:22.479
There are no cameras in the lab.

25:22.563 --> 25:24.815
They can't do anything
with just suspicions.

25:24.898 --> 25:26.734
They have no proof.

25:34.158 --> 25:36.577
And there's no way
they can trace the accounts.

25:39.371 --> 25:41.206
Go overseas for a while.

25:43.083 --> 25:46.128
I'll have a place ready for you
when things quiet down.

25:50.257 --> 25:51.967
Thank you.

25:56.513 --> 25:58.891
What should we do?
She looks very anxious.

25:59.850 --> 26:02.394
Wait for the right time
to take care of her quietly.

26:04.688 --> 26:06.815
The world truly has changed.

26:06.899 --> 26:08.901
This island of Tamna was infamous

26:08.984 --> 26:11.528
as a desolate place of exile,
reserved only for the worst traitors

26:11.612 --> 26:13.363
who plotted treason against the throne.

26:14.198 --> 26:16.075
How does this look like an exile site?

26:16.158 --> 26:17.451
It's a paradise resort.

26:17.534 --> 26:20.329
Jeju is too crowded now
to even be a resort.

26:20.412 --> 26:23.707
Maybe some deserted Pacific island
might come close to a retreat.

26:23.791 --> 26:24.750
Yeah.

26:25.334 --> 26:27.544
You might actually get
some rest somewhere like that.

26:27.628 --> 26:29.588
It gives off Mont Saint-Michel vibes.

26:31.340 --> 26:32.925
What? "Monsoon Seashell"?

26:34.384 --> 26:37.179
It's a rocky island
off the coast of Normandy, France.

26:37.262 --> 26:40.015
Is that Mont-whatever
a deserted island too?

26:40.099 --> 26:42.768
No, it only becomes
an island at high tide.

26:42.851 --> 26:43.852
It's pretty nice.

26:43.936 --> 26:45.938
If my new launch is a huge hit,

26:46.021 --> 26:47.689
I'm thinking of buying an island.

26:48.857 --> 26:50.984
A private island retreat
sounds nice, doesn't it?

26:51.068 --> 26:53.028
Forget about your Monsoon Seashells.

26:53.112 --> 26:55.197
I think Tamna is pretty nice already.

26:55.280 --> 26:57.116
Actually, I like it very much.

26:58.200 --> 27:00.035
First time in Jeju?

27:00.119 --> 27:02.037
-Bring it down a notch.
-It is my first time.

27:02.121 --> 27:04.206
It is my first time seeing the ocean.

27:08.335 --> 27:11.338
You live in a country surrounded
by water on three sides,

27:11.421 --> 27:12.840
and this is your first time?

27:15.300 --> 27:16.635
Cha Se-gye.

27:16.718 --> 27:18.595
You should try taking in
a deep breath too.

27:31.316 --> 27:33.986
If I had died without witnessing
this wonderful sight…

27:36.029 --> 27:37.614
it would have been my greatest regret.

27:59.344 --> 28:04.057
SEOGEON ISLAND
JEJU'S ISLAND OF MYSTERY

28:07.728 --> 28:10.939
Korea's very own Miracle of Moses.
The Seogeon Island Sea Parting.

28:12.357 --> 28:14.151
When you need to take a break.

28:14.818 --> 28:17.487
Are you on vacation too?
It's like we read each other's minds.

28:17.571 --> 28:19.406
Korea is full of amazing places.

28:19.489 --> 28:20.949
The sea parts at low tide.

28:21.491 --> 28:23.911
Maybe the Miracle of Moses
was just low tide.

28:51.271 --> 28:52.189
Gosh.

29:02.866 --> 29:03.825
Wait.

29:04.409 --> 29:05.661
There are brine stones here.

29:05.744 --> 29:07.621
-"Brine stone"?
-Brine stone.

29:08.205 --> 29:09.289
As in "pebble."

29:09.998 --> 29:12.000
Wasn't that your nickname?
Gravel? Pebble?

29:12.084 --> 29:13.502
Or something like that.

29:14.127 --> 29:15.420
What an absurd nickname.

29:15.504 --> 29:17.422
Instead of a measly pebble,

29:17.506 --> 29:18.799
I shall be a chunk of rock.

29:18.882 --> 29:19.946
If anyone messes with me,

29:20.046 --> 29:22.052
this chunk of rock
will come crashing down.

29:23.345 --> 29:26.098
Yeah. "Chunk of rock"
suits you better than "pebble."

29:31.687 --> 29:32.813
So salty!

29:32.896 --> 29:34.481
Did you think seawater would be sweet?

29:34.564 --> 29:35.649
Why would you taste that?

29:35.732 --> 29:36.692
I see.

29:37.401 --> 29:38.986
Seawater is quite salty.

29:47.035 --> 29:49.288
I am truly glad to be alive.

29:50.122 --> 29:51.790
The sea dyed by the sunset

29:52.916 --> 29:54.334
is ridiculously beautiful.

29:55.002 --> 29:57.379
You've been going on like some old lady.

29:57.462 --> 29:59.131
What, are you back from the dead?

30:01.425 --> 30:02.926
It is because I am happy.

30:04.886 --> 30:06.263
I am so happy to be alive.

30:43.300 --> 30:44.968
It's Yoon Ji-hyo.

30:47.512 --> 30:49.097
It's a private villa, right?

30:49.181 --> 30:51.391
I heard the security was airtight.

30:52.267 --> 30:53.393
She's pretty, right?

30:55.854 --> 30:57.814
I apologize.
Would you like a tour of the resort?

30:57.898 --> 30:59.566
Or to head straight to your room?

31:00.567 --> 31:01.568
To the room.

31:01.651 --> 31:03.070
Sure. Just give me a moment.

31:05.572 --> 31:07.532
Excuse me, but you can't film here.

31:07.616 --> 31:09.201
-Okay.
-Sorry about that.

31:12.162 --> 31:13.163
Shin Seo-ri?

31:13.997 --> 31:15.248
Cha and his aide?

31:15.332 --> 31:16.833
What a scandal.

31:17.876 --> 31:18.919
Wow.

31:19.628 --> 31:21.922
What do you want for dinner?
I can look for a place.

31:22.005 --> 31:24.841
Since we are by the sea,
let us eat ostrea.

31:24.925 --> 31:26.593
According to the Dongui Bogam,

31:26.676 --> 31:28.095
consuming it refines the skin

31:28.178 --> 31:29.971
and improves one's complexion.

31:30.055 --> 31:31.765
The finest tonic the sea has to offer.

31:31.848 --> 31:33.266
"Ostrea"? Is that a type of meat?

31:33.350 --> 31:34.976
You do not know what ostrea is?

31:35.060 --> 31:37.396
Its white, milky flesh tends
to be quite plump--

31:37.479 --> 31:38.688
Octopus?

31:39.356 --> 31:40.440
No, not that.

31:40.524 --> 31:42.025
It is sweet when grilled,

31:42.109 --> 31:44.277
and as a soup,
the broth is so refreshing.

31:44.361 --> 31:45.946
-Hairtail?
-No!

31:46.029 --> 31:49.199
You can eat the meat
and grind the leftover shells into powder

31:49.282 --> 31:50.992
that can be used to calm a racing heart

31:51.076 --> 31:52.953
and aid a man's nocturnal emissions.

31:53.036 --> 31:55.418
Both food and remedy,
not a single part wasted--

31:55.501 --> 31:57.582
Right. So what is it exactly?

31:57.666 --> 31:58.875
Could it be oysters?

31:58.959 --> 31:59.918
Oysters?

32:00.001 --> 32:01.795
My grandpa used to run an apothecary.

32:01.878 --> 32:03.755
Apothecaries call oysters "ostrea."

32:03.839 --> 32:06.299
Yes, that's it! Oysters. Ostrea.

32:06.383 --> 32:08.760
Just say it normally.
Did we really need to play 20 Questions?

32:08.844 --> 32:10.762
Do you really expect me
to solve all your riddles?

32:10.846 --> 32:12.139
Even if I speak like a fool,

32:12.222 --> 32:14.516
my servant should understand
like a genius.

32:14.599 --> 32:16.309
I can't eat oysters. Bad stomach.

32:16.393 --> 32:18.770
Nobody asked for the servant's opinion.

32:19.688 --> 32:20.981
Who's that?

32:28.071 --> 32:30.407
Shin Seo-ri, that loser, has a boyfriend?

32:31.950 --> 32:34.286
Is that guy Mr. Supercar?

32:34.369 --> 32:36.163
-How about black pork?
-Sounds good.

32:36.246 --> 32:38.707
We are by the sea, so we must eat ostrea.

32:38.790 --> 32:41.793
But he looks way too shabby to own one.

32:43.670 --> 32:46.256
Jeez. Who knew a trip to Tamna
would be so damn exhausting?

32:46.339 --> 32:48.341
Wow, it's so spacious.

32:48.425 --> 32:49.468
The TV is huge too.

32:49.551 --> 32:51.052
-You're late.
-Goodness me.

32:51.136 --> 32:52.137
What took you so long?

32:52.220 --> 32:54.681
Why are you so surprised?
Guilty conscience?

32:56.308 --> 32:59.060
Oh, you must be Seo-ri's manager.

32:59.144 --> 33:00.729
Gwang-nam, right?

33:00.812 --> 33:01.688
Right?

33:02.439 --> 33:03.482
Nice to meet you.

33:04.149 --> 33:06.067
Let's do some good work together.

33:07.194 --> 33:09.362
Oh right. The ad agency said

33:09.446 --> 33:10.989
Mr. Cha's team is staying here as well.

33:11.072 --> 33:12.741
Tell them I'll treat them to dinner.

33:12.824 --> 33:14.201
Yes, ma'am.

33:20.123 --> 33:22.584
Calling to invite them is bad manners.

33:22.667 --> 33:24.336
You must go and tell them in person.

33:24.419 --> 33:26.838
Making me run around like a dog.

33:30.717 --> 33:33.595
Seo-ri, where in the world
did you find a kid like him?

33:33.678 --> 33:35.722
Why are you here unannounced, Ms. Hong?

33:37.015 --> 33:38.892
Where the needle goes, the thread follows.

33:38.975 --> 33:41.061
Why wouldn't I be here for your shoot?

33:41.770 --> 33:44.523
I thought that minx
was your needle, not me.

33:44.606 --> 33:46.691
Ji-hyo is completely drained right now.

33:46.775 --> 33:48.360
She went far away to recharge.

33:48.985 --> 33:49.861
Far away?

33:50.403 --> 33:51.279
Where?

33:59.079 --> 34:01.414
Damn it. There are couples everywhere.

34:01.498 --> 34:03.083
Maybe I should've gone camping?

34:04.417 --> 34:06.169
-Wait.
-He says he just wants to rest.

34:06.253 --> 34:08.213
Okay, I'll pass that on.

34:09.047 --> 34:10.507
Hold on. You have some dust.

34:11.841 --> 34:13.426
-You're good now.
-Thank you.

34:14.135 --> 34:16.012
You have some on your back too.

34:16.096 --> 34:18.390
-Maybe he really is Mr. Supercar?
-Thanks.

34:22.060 --> 34:23.603
Wait, he's coming here.

34:23.687 --> 34:25.146
He's coming right towards me.

34:37.576 --> 34:38.493
What the…

34:51.214 --> 34:53.592
Hello, my name is Baek Gwang-nam.

34:53.675 --> 34:54.759
Excuse me?

34:54.843 --> 34:57.762
Well, it looked like you were on vacation,

34:57.846 --> 34:59.514
so I didn't want to bother you,

34:59.598 --> 35:02.309
but I gathered up the courage
and decided to say hi.

35:02.392 --> 35:04.019
Oh, I see.

35:04.102 --> 35:05.562
I'm a huge fan.

35:07.063 --> 35:10.191
I saw on Insta that you were on vacation,

35:10.275 --> 35:12.902
but I never expected
to run into you like this.

35:13.445 --> 35:14.529
You're a fan of mine?

35:14.613 --> 35:15.905
Yes, a huge fan.

35:17.032 --> 35:18.491
You're really heavenly in person.

35:19.451 --> 35:21.077
An angel on screen too.

35:22.579 --> 35:23.622
Right.

35:25.749 --> 35:27.250
I can't believe this.

35:27.876 --> 35:30.170
Well, do you want to take a selfie?

35:30.253 --> 35:32.922
I'm too nervous for that.
I don't think I could.

35:33.006 --> 35:34.466
Okay.

35:47.437 --> 35:49.105
At least he has a good eye.

35:50.190 --> 35:52.233
Hello, my name is Baek Gwang-nam.

35:54.944 --> 35:56.780
But…

35:56.863 --> 35:58.865
what's with the getup?

35:58.948 --> 36:00.492
Looking so raggedy.

36:01.117 --> 36:02.577
Or maybe it's vintage?

36:05.580 --> 36:07.791
They make a pretty good kimchi broth.

36:07.874 --> 36:09.334
We should've grilled some black pork.

36:09.417 --> 36:11.336
Why are we eating kimchi noodles?

36:11.419 --> 36:13.421
Let me know if you need anything else.

36:13.505 --> 36:14.798
I'll be right on it.

36:14.881 --> 36:16.007
That's enough.

36:16.091 --> 36:18.301
Just toast and be gone. I'm tired.

36:18.385 --> 36:20.595
-Okay. Cheers.
-Cheers.

36:22.889 --> 36:23.890
From now on,

36:23.973 --> 36:26.309
I intend to give this job
everything I have.

36:26.393 --> 36:27.602
Just leave it all to me.

36:29.062 --> 36:30.105
That's nice.

36:30.188 --> 36:32.148
We got this, Jeju Shoot Team!

36:33.024 --> 36:34.776
Have a good night!

36:39.239 --> 36:42.826
What's gotten into him?
He just suddenly decided to stop sulking?

36:42.909 --> 36:45.120
The human mind will forever elude us.

36:45.203 --> 36:46.162
I could not care less.

36:47.747 --> 36:50.041
Anyway, to finish what I was saying.

36:50.125 --> 36:53.128
The concept for this shoot is
"Jeju Goddess."

36:53.211 --> 36:54.212
No.

36:54.295 --> 36:55.964
Is she possessed by the spirit of nudity?

36:56.047 --> 36:58.425
I mean, is she dressed or naked?

36:58.508 --> 36:59.801
That is profoundly vulgar.

36:59.884 --> 37:02.095
That's exactly the point.

37:02.178 --> 37:03.596
Look. Barely there.

37:03.680 --> 37:05.348
Almost see-through. You know?

37:05.432 --> 37:07.392
Look at Greek mythology.

37:07.976 --> 37:10.562
They're all butt-naked
and staring right at you.

37:10.645 --> 37:12.147
Gods have no shame.

37:12.230 --> 37:14.149
That's just how they are.

37:14.899 --> 37:16.609
-Really?
-Yeah.

37:18.069 --> 37:20.947
Our bodies will just rot away
when we die anyway.

37:21.573 --> 37:24.993
We must use our beauty at its peak
to make it worthwhile.

37:25.076 --> 37:26.077
Exactly.

37:26.703 --> 37:28.288
All right. If I am doing this,

37:28.371 --> 37:30.915
I might as well
go all out and show it all off.

37:30.999 --> 37:32.083
That's the spirit.

37:32.167 --> 37:33.168
Cheers.

37:48.933 --> 37:50.351
You look a bit pale, sir.

37:51.019 --> 37:53.271
Yeah. I just didn't sleep well last night.

37:53.354 --> 37:56.191
You should be resting at the hotel.
Why are you out here?

37:57.650 --> 37:59.694
Never mind that. Where's the model?

38:00.653 --> 38:01.529
There…

38:03.198 --> 38:04.866
she is. Ms. Shin Seo-ri.

38:31.559 --> 38:32.936
Hello.

38:33.019 --> 38:35.730
-Hello.
-Hello there.

38:36.523 --> 38:39.484
They weren't kidding.
The clothes really do make the person.

38:42.445 --> 38:44.364
What do you think, Mr. Cha?

38:56.376 --> 38:58.628
Don't you think
that outfit is a bit too much?

38:58.711 --> 39:00.588
You must be kidding, Mr. Cha.

39:00.672 --> 39:02.549
She looks absolutely gorgeous.

39:02.632 --> 39:05.134
Seo-ri, maybe we can try
moving around a bit. Yeah.

39:12.559 --> 39:14.102
Change her outfit. Right now.

39:14.727 --> 39:16.938
-Please go change.
-Let's go change.

39:27.282 --> 39:29.993
The design is too haute couture. Next.

39:31.202 --> 39:32.662
We'll be right back.

39:40.587 --> 39:42.797
And this one is too prêt-à-porter.

39:42.881 --> 39:44.007
Swap.

39:52.807 --> 39:55.685
I mean,
what's up with all these clothes?

39:56.603 --> 39:58.646
I don't even know where to look.

39:58.730 --> 40:00.440
Am I some mutt you are trying to train?

40:00.523 --> 40:01.858
-Your eyes are the issue.
-Come on.

40:01.941 --> 40:03.568
Are your eyes possessed or something?

40:03.651 --> 40:05.778
-Stop it.
-Let go of me! Why, that little…

40:07.280 --> 40:08.156
Hold on.

40:08.698 --> 40:10.408
-Manager Baek!
-No, let's not do that.

40:11.492 --> 40:13.411
Come on, Mr. Cha.

40:14.078 --> 40:16.998
The marketing team signed off
on the final concept,

40:17.081 --> 40:20.543
and you personally approved these outfits.

40:20.627 --> 40:22.545
You can't just change them suddenly.

40:22.629 --> 40:25.131
The photos didn't show the fabric quality.

40:25.214 --> 40:27.216
This is an ad campaign,
not a personal photo shoot.

40:27.300 --> 40:29.552
The model stands out
way too much right now.

40:31.638 --> 40:33.306
She doesn't stand out that much.

40:33.389 --> 40:35.016
Her very being stands out too much.

40:35.099 --> 40:37.101
The outfit suits the location well.

40:37.185 --> 40:38.478
Screw the location.

40:38.561 --> 40:40.730
She's the only thing I can see right now!

40:43.107 --> 40:45.360
It looks fine. What's wrong with him?

40:45.443 --> 40:46.903
Why can't he just approve it?

40:51.866 --> 40:54.786
Replace all the outfits
and get my approval again.

40:54.869 --> 40:57.330
I'm the advertiser,
so you should meet my needs.

40:57.413 --> 40:58.539
Yes, sir.

41:01.584 --> 41:03.127
Why are my legs so numb?

41:09.801 --> 41:12.261
The person you are trying
to reach is unavailable…

41:15.306 --> 41:17.016
Ms. An Seong-hui, are you home?

41:19.477 --> 41:20.645
Ms. An Seong-hui?

41:21.270 --> 41:23.272
I'm from Biojei.

41:24.899 --> 41:26.609
Ms. An Seong-hui, are you home?

41:28.820 --> 41:29.988
Ms. An Seong-hui?

41:33.074 --> 41:35.118
We handled the nurse as instructed.

41:35.201 --> 41:36.577
How did Cha Se-gye react?

41:36.661 --> 41:38.913
Without proof, it seems he decided

41:38.997 --> 41:40.373
to stick to his schedule.

41:40.456 --> 41:41.889
Word from the set is a bit strange.

41:41.958 --> 41:44.711
He began interfering heavily
before shooting even began,

41:44.794 --> 41:46.421
causing some friction.

41:46.504 --> 41:49.090
He kept changing the model's outfits,

41:49.173 --> 41:50.800
upsetting the crew.

41:51.384 --> 41:52.593
Changing outfits?

41:55.555 --> 41:56.431
How amusing.

42:00.184 --> 42:01.144
It seems

42:02.729 --> 42:04.605
the time has come.

42:08.901 --> 42:11.738
Excuse me,
can I ask you for a little help?

42:11.821 --> 42:13.906
My grandson got lost.

42:13.990 --> 42:14.907
Your grandson?

42:17.035 --> 42:19.829
I am not so meddlesome that I would go
searching for some stranger's kid.

42:19.912 --> 42:21.748
I'll make it worth your while.

42:21.831 --> 42:24.333
Here. This is licorice taffy.

42:24.417 --> 42:26.252
Boiled with honey for three days.

42:26.335 --> 42:27.795
I'll give you this too.

42:28.504 --> 42:29.881
NODO MANAGER BAEK GWANG-NAM

42:40.016 --> 42:41.976
WE DISCOVERED THE QUEEN OF DYNAESTIE
GREAT JOB, EVERYONE!

42:43.186 --> 42:44.520
Is Seo-ri still not answering?

42:44.604 --> 42:46.856
I called over ten times
and checked her room.

42:46.939 --> 42:47.857
I can't find her.

42:47.940 --> 42:50.777
Then you should send people out
to find her. What are you doing?

42:50.860 --> 42:52.153
Don't worry.

42:52.236 --> 42:54.197
Maybe she went to get a snack--

42:54.280 --> 42:57.492
Where's she going this late
when she doesn't even know her way around?

42:58.910 --> 43:00.328
You should stay here, sir.

43:00.411 --> 43:02.580
It'll only make her look bad
if you leave now.

43:02.663 --> 43:04.457
The crew is already upset over the delays

43:04.540 --> 43:06.709
caused by all the wardrobe changes.

43:06.793 --> 43:08.461
It'll only start weird rumors.

43:11.798 --> 43:13.007
What do I…

43:14.258 --> 43:16.135
All right. Thanks.

43:18.221 --> 43:19.514
Sir, can we step outside?

43:21.182 --> 43:24.644
Ms. Kim found her and is taking her
to a nearby hospital.

43:24.727 --> 43:25.937
And the nurse's current state?

43:26.020 --> 43:27.438
They say she's stable,

43:27.522 --> 43:30.274
but she hasn't woken up yet,
so we have to wait.

43:41.494 --> 43:43.287
Sir, where are you…

43:43.871 --> 43:47.625
Our policy prohibits sharing this footage
with the guests.

43:47.708 --> 43:50.253
But since you said it's an emergency…

43:51.045 --> 43:52.171
-Stop there.
-What?

43:52.255 --> 43:54.173
-Bottom right, third one.
-Here?

44:10.940 --> 44:14.318
I mean, this is like
finding a needle in a haystack.

44:14.986 --> 44:16.863
We should let your family know

44:17.738 --> 44:19.866
or get more men to help out.

44:19.949 --> 44:22.535
If it is just us,
we will end up going in circles all night.

44:22.618 --> 44:24.370
Gosh, I am sorry.

44:24.453 --> 44:26.164
We shouldn't have rushed here.

44:26.789 --> 44:30.042
You're going through
all this trouble because of me.

44:30.793 --> 44:31.919
My goodness.

44:32.461 --> 44:33.379
Wait.

44:34.046 --> 44:36.507
-Jeez. What happened?
-Oh no.

44:38.342 --> 44:39.760
Don't worry.

44:39.844 --> 44:41.679
I'll make you a fresh batch.

44:43.139 --> 44:45.183
Never mind that. Think carefully.

44:45.266 --> 44:46.809
Whereabouts did he let go of your hand?

44:46.893 --> 44:47.894
I'm sure

44:48.519 --> 44:49.896
it was around here

44:50.563 --> 44:52.273
that he disappeared.

44:53.232 --> 44:54.108
Goodness.

44:54.192 --> 44:55.818
How old is your grandson?

44:55.902 --> 44:57.820
He's 6 years old.

44:57.904 --> 45:00.281
My Hyeon-ho is 6.

45:00.364 --> 45:02.241
You look to be at least 80,

45:02.325 --> 45:04.160
but your grandson is only 6?

45:05.328 --> 45:07.205
How old are you, old man?

45:07.288 --> 45:08.915
Old man? What do you mean?

45:08.998 --> 45:10.833
I just got married early.

45:10.917 --> 45:13.294
I'm only 55 years old.

45:15.588 --> 45:16.672
Fifty-five?

45:22.345 --> 45:23.471
Grandpa!

45:24.388 --> 45:25.556
What are you doing?

45:32.104 --> 45:33.272
Mom and Dad

45:33.356 --> 45:35.149
went to the police to find you.

45:35.233 --> 45:36.484
Where have you been?

45:37.860 --> 45:39.028
Who are you?

45:41.197 --> 45:43.115
Gosh, I'm so sorry.

45:43.199 --> 45:44.367
My grandfather came to see me…

45:44.450 --> 45:45.326
SONG HYEON-HO

45:45.409 --> 45:46.786
…and must have gotten lost.

45:48.329 --> 45:50.665
Your party was looking for you.

45:52.166 --> 45:54.794
Grandpa! Where are you going now?

45:58.564 --> 45:59.440
Could it be dotage?

45:59.524 --> 46:00.399
DOTAGE: DEMENTIA

46:00.466 --> 46:01.759
SEORI'S NOODLE SHOP

46:01.842 --> 46:02.969
My goodness.

46:08.641 --> 46:10.518
Her after school class
should've ended by now.

46:10.601 --> 46:12.561
What's taking her so long?

46:13.312 --> 46:15.064
She must be hungry.

47:10.828 --> 47:12.163
Hello, sir.

47:12.246 --> 47:13.414
I'm a bit busy right now.

47:13.497 --> 47:15.458
Did your guest make it back okay?

47:15.541 --> 47:17.126
You saw her? Where?

47:17.835 --> 47:20.254
We would've been in serious trouble
without her help.

47:20.338 --> 47:21.881
My grandfather got lost--

47:21.964 --> 47:24.091
Where is she right now?

47:24.884 --> 47:25.885
I saw her earlier

47:25.968 --> 47:27.887
in the woods near the beach,
but I'm not sure…

47:27.970 --> 47:28.971
Damn it.

47:58.000 --> 47:59.752
Why she brought in someone like you…

48:12.181 --> 48:14.058
Is anyone out there?

48:14.141 --> 48:15.351
Please help me!

49:20.458 --> 49:22.626
Are you okay? Are you hurt anywhere?

49:31.093 --> 49:33.429
Why are you suddenly trying to be a hero?

49:33.512 --> 49:35.764
You don't know the area.
How could you have found anyone?

49:35.848 --> 49:38.309
I was not trying to be a hero.

49:39.226 --> 49:40.936
The old man kept clinging to me.

49:41.020 --> 49:44.398
You're not the type to just accept
anyone who latches on. Why help?

49:44.482 --> 49:46.358
Why are you suddenly such a busybody?

49:50.404 --> 49:52.198
Why do you care if I am being

49:53.407 --> 49:54.575
a busybody or not?

49:54.658 --> 49:55.618
Of course I care.

49:55.701 --> 49:58.662
We're on a business trip.
You can't just go off on your own.

49:58.746 --> 49:59.997
Do not be angry.

50:00.998 --> 50:02.249
What did I do so wrong--

50:02.333 --> 50:03.709
You were wrong

50:03.792 --> 50:06.378
to blindly follow a stranger at night.

50:06.462 --> 50:08.380
What if something happened to you?

50:13.093 --> 50:16.263
Are you this angry
because you were worried about me?

50:16.347 --> 50:17.932
Because I could have been hurt?

50:18.724 --> 50:21.018
Don't twist my words.
Keep work and private life separate.

50:21.101 --> 50:23.854
You were late for work
because of your personal actions.

50:23.938 --> 50:26.023
A nuisance to your colleagues.
Am I wrong?

50:26.815 --> 50:27.733
A nuisance?

50:28.234 --> 50:30.569
Yes. Poking around everywhere

50:30.653 --> 50:32.613
and meddling all day.

50:32.696 --> 50:35.366
Professionally, it's an obstruction.
Privately, it's a waste of time.

50:35.449 --> 50:37.493
So please! God damn it.

50:38.494 --> 50:40.746
Just stay out of trouble, please.

50:47.586 --> 50:49.171
Very well, I understand.

50:49.255 --> 50:50.923
I shall take care not to be a nuisance.

50:51.006 --> 50:53.842
So do not come looking for me
like this next time.

50:53.926 --> 50:56.762
I too shall treat you
as a complete stranger from now on.

51:10.651 --> 51:11.777
Great work, everyone.

51:29.336 --> 51:31.589
-May I have your attention, please?
-Yes.

51:31.672 --> 51:34.008
Please let me apologize.
My grandfather lost his way,

51:34.091 --> 51:35.926
but Ms. Shin Seo-ri helped me find him.

51:36.010 --> 51:37.595
That was what made her late.

51:40.598 --> 51:42.016
Is that true?

51:42.099 --> 51:44.143
Well, I did not exactly help find him.

51:44.226 --> 51:46.979
Do you break out in hives
when you do good deeds?

51:47.062 --> 51:49.106
His grandson confirmed it.
Why keep denying it?

51:49.189 --> 51:51.358
Please allow me to offer
a bottle of Premier Cru Burgundy

51:51.442 --> 51:53.527
for each table.

51:55.362 --> 51:56.614
-Wow.
-Wow.

51:58.866 --> 52:01.994
-Shin Seo-ri!
-Shin Seo-ri!

52:02.077 --> 52:04.830
-Shin Seo-ri!
-Shin Seo-ri!

52:04.913 --> 52:06.957
-Thank you for the wine!
-Shin Seo-ri!

52:08.667 --> 52:10.836
Thank you for the wine!

52:20.387 --> 52:22.264
Now, have you ever heard of it?

52:22.348 --> 52:24.683
This has gone unrecorded for 500 years.

52:24.767 --> 52:26.477
It is the Chaos Wine of Joseon.

52:26.560 --> 52:29.855
Makgeolli mixed with wine.
The perfect harmony of East and West.

52:30.397 --> 52:32.316
And I am the only one who can brew it.

52:35.361 --> 52:36.445
Drink up!

52:36.528 --> 52:38.197
-Drink up!
-Drink up!

52:51.043 --> 52:52.753
I'm not drinking tonight.

52:52.836 --> 52:54.088
Come on.

52:54.171 --> 52:56.715
Drink, Mr. Son! Drink!

52:56.799 --> 52:58.634
-Drink!
-Drink!

52:58.717 --> 53:01.887
-Down the hatch! Chug!
-Down the hatch! Chug!

53:01.970 --> 53:03.555
-Chug!
-Chug!

53:03.639 --> 53:06.263
-How long will you make us dance?
-How long will you make us dance?

53:06.350 --> 53:07.226
Mr. Son.

53:07.309 --> 53:09.561
-Look at my dislocated shoulders!
-Look at my dislocated shoulders!

53:09.645 --> 53:10.521
Mr. Son!

53:10.604 --> 53:12.356
-Wow!
-Wow!

53:14.483 --> 53:15.776
Wait!

53:15.859 --> 53:17.903
Michelin class? No?

53:22.825 --> 53:24.785
I'll have one more. This is so good.

53:24.868 --> 53:26.578
-Mr. Son.
-Yes, Michelin.

53:26.662 --> 53:28.956
Isn't this after-party
an extension of work?

53:29.039 --> 53:30.499
Pace yourself.

53:32.042 --> 53:33.627
No fun!

53:34.253 --> 53:35.295
What are you even doing?

53:35.379 --> 53:37.131
Not drinking at a drinking party,

53:37.214 --> 53:39.800
just sitting around chattering
like a petty little miser.

53:40.843 --> 53:43.011
You should have a glass too, Lord CEO.

53:43.971 --> 53:47.850
-Drink!
-Drink!

53:47.933 --> 53:51.520
-Drink!
-Drink!

53:51.603 --> 53:53.313
I'm not drinking.

53:53.939 --> 53:55.190
Come on, drink.

53:56.066 --> 53:58.694
Being the only sober one
among drunks is no fun.

53:58.777 --> 54:00.821
I'm more comfortable
being sober and boring.

54:01.655 --> 54:04.199
It is not about comfort.
You just cannot drink.

54:04.283 --> 54:05.826
The petty little miser cannot handle

54:05.909 --> 54:07.536
a glass of Chaos Wine and chatters away.

54:07.619 --> 54:10.080
I told you it's not that I can't.
I just don't want to.

54:10.164 --> 54:11.957
Didn't you say you'd treat me
like a stranger?

54:12.040 --> 54:15.294
We may be strangers in private,
but not professionally.

54:15.377 --> 54:17.171
The lightweight who talks a big game.

54:17.254 --> 54:18.422
I am choosing not to drink.

54:18.505 --> 54:20.215
If you are that scared, let me.

54:20.299 --> 54:21.925
Hand it over.

54:22.009 --> 54:23.218
Who says I'm scared?

54:31.977 --> 54:34.396
-What a man!
-One more!

54:34.480 --> 54:37.399
You can drink just fine,
yet you put up such a fuss.

54:37.483 --> 54:39.860
You should have just tossed it back
like that from the start.

54:39.943 --> 54:43.614
Lord CEO,
you sure love playing hard to get.

54:54.958 --> 54:57.336
Right, why take things so seriously?

54:57.419 --> 54:59.963
I get to be this drunk because I am alive.

55:00.047 --> 55:02.966
Worldly anguish,
pointless worries and the like

55:03.050 --> 55:05.761
can all be washed away
with a single drink.

55:12.643 --> 55:14.478
Once a gloomy day passes,

55:14.561 --> 55:16.814
a pleasant new sun is bound to rise.

55:16.897 --> 55:19.733
Gosh, why is it so cold?

55:26.907 --> 55:28.992
Dawn is still a long way away.

55:31.578 --> 55:33.163
And where am I now?

55:37.000 --> 55:39.419
Where did everyone run off to without me?

55:39.503 --> 55:41.880
And you wonder
why I can't take my eyes off you?

55:44.675 --> 55:46.385
A stranger is speaking to me.

55:47.302 --> 55:49.429
Do you know me? I do not recognize you.

55:50.806 --> 55:52.307
You're drunk, Shin Seo-ri.

55:55.602 --> 55:56.603
Drunk, my foot.

55:57.354 --> 55:58.689
I am perfectly sober.

55:58.772 --> 56:00.691
Here, look how perfectly sober I am.

56:02.901 --> 56:04.236
I told you to watch it!

56:05.112 --> 56:06.697
Watch that degenerate behavior!

56:24.214 --> 56:25.716
"The moon rises, luminous."

56:26.300 --> 56:27.551
"The beauty, how lovely."

56:28.302 --> 56:30.053
"Gracefully entwining, unfolding."

56:30.137 --> 56:31.638
"My troubled heart…"

56:33.432 --> 56:36.768
"The bright moon rises,
revealing my beautiful love."

56:37.311 --> 56:39.271
"My heart aches in longing."

56:42.357 --> 56:43.775
Cha Se-gye.

56:44.359 --> 56:46.028
I must go to Mount Halla,

56:46.778 --> 56:48.906
-so lead the way.
-Why Mount Halla?

56:48.989 --> 56:51.533
I have something to say there.

56:52.659 --> 56:53.911
I must declare

56:53.994 --> 56:56.872
that I shall cast myself away
and live as Shin Seo-ri.

56:57.414 --> 57:00.542
Must you make that declaration
at Mount Halla, at this hour?

57:00.626 --> 57:01.585
Silence!

57:02.169 --> 57:03.587
Do you truly not know?

57:03.670 --> 57:05.714
My Lovely Sam Soon, Episode 12.

57:06.340 --> 57:08.884
Sam-soon cleanses herself
of her tedious past

57:08.967 --> 57:11.637
and declares her new life
as Kim Hee-jin.

57:11.720 --> 57:13.972
That very scene struck
a chord in my heart.

57:15.724 --> 57:17.684
With Mount Halla so close at hand,

57:17.768 --> 57:20.228
I cannot miss such a golden opportunity.

57:20.938 --> 57:22.648
What are you talking about?

57:22.731 --> 57:24.149
Shush. Let us go to Mount Halla!

57:24.232 --> 57:25.442
I'm not going to Mount Halla.

57:26.902 --> 57:28.820
Are you asking for palanquin fare?

57:30.864 --> 57:32.199
Here.

57:37.746 --> 57:39.623
When did you pick this up?

57:47.381 --> 57:49.883
No! Stop! My token!

57:49.967 --> 57:52.135
Are you nuts? Where are you going?

57:52.219 --> 57:54.554
Why did you throw away my precious token?

57:54.638 --> 57:55.847
I intended to cherish it.

57:55.931 --> 57:57.224
You just said it was my fare.

57:57.307 --> 57:59.184
Are you drunk?
Why would I pay with a rock?

57:59.267 --> 58:00.435
It must be you who is drunk.

58:00.519 --> 58:03.183
I stopped you going to Mount Halla,
even when you were freaking out.

58:03.283 --> 58:05.458
Are you mad?
Climbing a mountain in the dead of night?

58:05.533 --> 58:08.276
That's what I'm saying!
The sea is better than a mountain.

58:12.698 --> 58:14.116
You said you liked the sea.

58:15.826 --> 58:17.494
Just sober up a bit before we go.

58:19.538 --> 58:20.914
Very well, then.

58:25.919 --> 58:27.004
Cha Se-gye!

58:29.881 --> 58:31.216
Look at that.

59:04.458 --> 59:05.459
Hello.

59:08.378 --> 59:09.379
Ms. Mo Tae-hee.

59:16.803 --> 59:18.930
The sea has parted in two.

59:19.014 --> 59:21.099
Maybe I drank too much Chaos Wine?

59:21.183 --> 59:23.185
I told you yesterday. It's low tide.

59:23.268 --> 59:26.146
It becomes a path at ebb tide
and an island at high tide.

59:26.229 --> 59:27.731
It must be nice to be so smart,

59:27.814 --> 59:29.107
knowing everything in the world.

59:29.191 --> 59:31.610
Don't you think there's just too much
you don't know?

59:31.693 --> 59:34.196
Yet there is one thing I know for certain.

59:35.072 --> 59:36.656
How to endure life.

59:37.824 --> 59:41.078
To ensure good memories
are not easily forgotten,

59:42.120 --> 59:44.372
one must collect tokens like this.

59:46.124 --> 59:48.293
I have tucked away the fond memory

59:48.877 --> 59:50.420
of seeing the sea for the first time.

59:50.504 --> 59:52.506
When life becomes unbearable,

59:53.048 --> 59:54.591
I shall reach deep down

59:55.300 --> 59:57.719
and pull out the memories
of those good times.

59:58.887 --> 01:00:00.847
What if the good memories make you sad?

01:00:03.767 --> 01:00:04.935
What then?

01:00:06.520 --> 01:00:08.313
A memory both good and sad?

01:00:09.981 --> 01:00:11.441
You must tuck it back away.

01:00:11.983 --> 01:00:14.444
Since recalling it
will only make you weak,

01:00:14.986 --> 01:00:16.738
you must replace it with new ones.

01:00:22.035 --> 01:00:23.120
You…

01:00:25.080 --> 01:00:26.498
feel guilty, do you not?

01:00:29.042 --> 01:00:30.043
What?

01:00:31.670 --> 01:00:33.338
It is written all over your face.

01:00:34.673 --> 01:00:36.133
That you feel sorry.

01:00:36.216 --> 01:00:38.343
That you regret losing
your temper earlier.

01:00:41.263 --> 01:00:42.597
But it is quite all right.

01:00:43.223 --> 01:00:46.101
That is how people naturally act
when they are frightened.

01:00:46.977 --> 01:00:49.020
Even a man can easily become frightened.

01:00:49.604 --> 01:00:51.064
You need not feel sorry.

01:01:01.825 --> 01:01:03.743
No, I'm not sorry at all.

01:01:05.912 --> 01:01:07.038
If I had to go back,

01:01:07.122 --> 01:01:09.666
I would still chase after you
like a madman.

01:01:09.749 --> 01:01:12.502
I'd do something foolish
and blow up at you again.

01:01:13.336 --> 01:01:17.090
Even if you're disappointed in me,
as long as you're okay, I'll be relieved.

01:01:17.757 --> 01:01:19.843
This man is hopeless.

01:01:19.926 --> 01:01:21.803
I'm really sorry for being like this.

01:01:22.387 --> 01:01:25.640
A foolish man
who cannot even apologize properly.

01:01:26.766 --> 01:01:28.894
But I can't help it.
This is how I truly feel.

01:01:28.977 --> 01:01:31.062
A bull-headed lone wolf
who only cares about himself.

01:01:31.146 --> 01:01:32.480
Willful and self-centered.

01:01:32.981 --> 01:01:35.317
Shameless enough to sell
his conscience for money.

01:01:35.400 --> 01:01:36.735
So I'm warning you.

01:01:38.153 --> 01:01:40.280
Listen carefully to what I'm about to say.

01:01:43.408 --> 01:01:45.118
I'm about to do something,

01:01:45.202 --> 01:01:47.287
so if you want to run, now's your chance.

01:01:49.039 --> 01:01:50.457
I'll give you three seconds.

01:01:51.333 --> 01:01:52.542
One.

01:01:53.335 --> 01:01:54.419
Two.

01:01:55.503 --> 01:01:56.630
Three.

01:02:02.844 --> 01:02:05.764
There are countless reasons
I must not fall for this man.

01:02:22.072 --> 01:02:24.115
But there is just one reason

01:02:25.909 --> 01:02:27.160
why I have.

01:02:30.121 --> 01:02:31.790
You grabbed me first.

01:03:26.469 --> 01:03:29.806
MY ROYAL NEMESIS

01:03:30.557 --> 01:03:33.643
"The moon rises, luminous.
The beauty, how lovely."

01:03:33.727 --> 01:03:36.646
"Gracefully entwining, unfolding.
My troubled heart aches."

01:03:41.776 --> 01:03:43.403
"The bright moon rises,

01:03:43.486 --> 01:03:45.238
revealing my beautiful love."

01:03:45.322 --> 01:03:47.407
"It tenderly stirs and blooms."

01:03:50.243 --> 01:03:51.870
"My heart

01:03:51.953 --> 01:03:53.538
aches in longing."

01:03:58.043 --> 01:03:59.085
What?

01:04:05.425 --> 01:04:07.135
-Such irreverence.
-Gosh.

01:04:07.218 --> 01:04:10.972
A junior court lady who has only just had
her initiation is sneaking alcohol?

01:04:11.056 --> 01:04:13.808
Your Highness.
What brings you here this late…

01:04:13.892 --> 01:04:16.978
I came to chase away
the bird chittering through the night.

01:04:17.062 --> 01:04:19.147
And I find a palace attendant who drinks

01:04:19.230 --> 01:04:21.232
inside the palace
in defiance of the liquor ban?

01:04:21.316 --> 01:04:23.276
Do you have a death wish?

01:04:23.360 --> 01:04:25.070
No, it is not that.

01:04:25.945 --> 01:04:27.322
This is…

01:04:27.405 --> 01:04:29.699
This is not alcohol. It is medicine.

01:04:29.783 --> 01:04:32.118
-Medicine?
-Yes, it is medicine.

01:04:32.202 --> 01:04:35.580
I picked the ingredients myself
in the scorching summer heat to brew

01:04:36.373 --> 01:04:37.374
this fine medicine.

01:04:37.457 --> 01:04:41.252
Medicinal liquor for the ailing
is exempt from the ban.

01:04:41.336 --> 01:04:42.754
Is that what you mean?

01:04:42.837 --> 01:04:44.923
Then tell me, my companion.

01:04:45.673 --> 01:04:47.884
What ails you to drink
this medicinal liquor?

01:04:48.635 --> 01:04:49.969
Well,

01:04:50.053 --> 01:04:51.221
you see…

01:04:53.014 --> 01:04:54.974
I suffer greatly from suppressed anger,

01:04:55.642 --> 01:04:57.477
so I use alcohol as medicine.

01:04:58.269 --> 01:05:00.688
Rather than being consumed
by this rage within,

01:05:00.772 --> 01:05:02.315
is it not better to drink

01:05:03.149 --> 01:05:04.734
and stay alive?

01:05:06.152 --> 01:05:07.487
That mouth of yours

01:05:08.154 --> 01:05:10.240
is just too smart for its own good.

01:05:11.199 --> 01:05:14.035
-Stop smiling.
-You complained when I looked too grim.

01:05:14.911 --> 01:05:16.579
Now you scold me for smiling?

01:05:16.663 --> 01:05:18.415
Yes, stop smiling.

01:05:19.833 --> 01:05:21.042
You look ugly.

01:06:12.844 --> 01:06:13.970
A deserted island?

01:06:14.053 --> 01:06:16.681
I have not committed any sins.
Why have I been exiled here?

01:06:16.764 --> 01:06:17.807
There's nothing we can do.

01:06:17.891 --> 01:06:19.476
We'll just have to make
a cozy little life together.

01:06:19.559 --> 01:06:20.441
I have no memory of that.

01:06:20.511 --> 01:06:22.353
You will never be able
to take back what happened yesterday.

01:06:22.437 --> 01:06:24.010
I really need to quit drinking.

01:06:24.085 --> 01:06:27.233
Let's shoot him down
when he reaches the apex.

01:06:27.317 --> 01:06:28.234
D-Day should be…

01:06:28.318 --> 01:06:29.819
What's your relationship with Se-gye?

01:06:29.903 --> 01:06:31.905
Se-gye and I are going to be married.

01:06:31.988 --> 01:06:33.823
Goodness! Ma'am!

01:06:33.907 --> 01:06:36.451
Mr. Cha, did you drive
under the influence?

01:06:36.534 --> 01:06:38.495
Do what you must to keep her
out of the press.

01:06:38.578 --> 01:06:40.371
Just stop doing anything for me.

01:06:40.455 --> 01:06:41.831
If you keep making me waver,

01:06:41.915 --> 01:06:44.501
I will shamelessly start hoping for more.

01:06:46.920 --> 01:06:48.922
Subtitle translation by Justin S. Kim
